	<description>Since the death of her husband, Anne Dunne and her three children have struggled in every way. In a last ditch effort to save the family, Anne plans an elaborate sailing vacation to bring everyone together once again. But only an hour out of port, everything is going wrong. The teenage daughter, Carrie, is planning to drown herself. The teenage son, Mark, is high on drugs and ten-year-old Ernie is nearly catatonic. This is the worst vacation ever.&lt;p&gt;Anne manages to pull things together bit by bit, but just as they begin feeling like a family again, something catastrophic happens. Survival may be the least of their concerns. &lt;br /&gt;Written with the blistering pace and shocking twists that only James Patterson can master, &lt;i&gt;Sail&lt;/i&gt; takes "Lost" and "Survivor" to a new level of terror.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
